{"id":"edc57f8768e4be99f430eac8f3fdd609031d6d8b","axis":"silent","repo":"rustwasm/wasm-bindgen","sha":"edc57f8768e4be99f430eac8f3fdd609031d6d8b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -51,6 +51,17 @@","   [#5410](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5410)","   [#5423](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5423)"," ","+* `Nullable<T>` converts into `JsValue` with `From`, `Null` becoming `null`","+  as `None` becomes `undefined` for `Option<T>`, and `Option<T>`,","+  `Nullable<T>` and `Result<T, E>` are `Promising` for any `T: Promising`,","+  so a `Promise<Nullable<JsString>>` awaits to a `Nullable<JsString>`.","+  `String` and `&str` upcast to `JsValue`, and `String` to itself, so a","+  `Promise<String>` from an `experimental_generic_mono` import is `JsGeneric`","+  and upcasts to `Promise<JsValue>` as `Promise<bool>` does. Together these","+  make a `Promise<Nullable<JsString>>` or `Promise<String>` from a mono","+  import usable wherever a promise is expected.","+  [#5427](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5427)","+"," * Added `MaybeIntoWasmAbi` / `MaybeFromWasmAbi`, the ABI of `Option<T>` for","   every `T`, with an associated `MaybeAbi` that lets a type without a spare","   value in its own ABI, such as `i32` or `f64`, pick a wider one. `Option<T>`","@@ -165,6 +176,31 @@"," "," ### Changed"," ","+* The js-sys `JsFunction*` traits' associated types (`Ret`, `ArgN`, `BindN`)","+  no longer carry a `JsGeneric` bound, so a `Function<fn(..)>` signature may","+  name a converted carrier such as `Nullable<JsString>`, and","+  `Function::from_closure` accepts a closure with converted arguments. Generic","+  code over these traits that calls `call*` or `bind*` now needs the bound","+  itself, as `where F::Ret: JsGeneric, F::Arg1: JsGeneric`. The hidden","+  `PromiseTuple` trait's `Joined` and `Settled` likewise drop it, its","+  Rust-tuple impl packing the promise handles directly rather than upcasting","+  each, and the","+  `JsGeneric` bounds that only existed to satisfy a `Function<fn(..)>` slot","+  or to tag a type argument are gone: `Promising for Promise<T, E>`,","+  `Promise::new_typed`, the `PromiseWithResolvers` `resolve`/`reject`","+  getters, the `PropertyDescriptor` `get`/`set` accessors, `WeakMap::new` and","+  the `entries`/`from_entries` family of `Array`, `Set`, `Map` and `Object`.","+  [#5427](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5427)","+","+* `Option<T>: TryFromJsValue` now reads `null` as `None`, as the `Option<T>`","+  ABI does, so `Option::<JsValue>::try_from_js_value(JsValue::NULL)` is","+  `None` where it was `Some(null)`. A `T` that accepts `null` as a distinct","+  value space sets the new `TryFromJsValue::NULLABLE` const, as","+  `Nullable<T>` does, and an `Option` of it passes `null` through, so","+  `Option<Nullable<T>>` reads it as `Some(Nullable::Null)`. `Nullable<T>`","+  itself converts from a `JsValue` with `TryFromJsValue`.","+  [#5427](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5427)","+"," * With reference types, `static_string` constants and the reserved","   `undefined`, `null`, `true` and `false` values are stored at fixed slots of","   the `externref` table, which is now sized to include them, and cloning or"],"additions":36,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/cli/tests/reference/async-import.bg.js","lines":["@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ export function __wbg_call_a48f35d3fb7572a8() { return handleError(function (arg","     const ret = arg0.call(arg1, arg2);","     return ret;"," }, arguments); }","-export function __wbg_new_typed_1b466b4a87f4f6fa(arg0, arg1) {","+export function __wbg_new_typed_7923e8c495a7fb41(arg0, arg1) {","     try {","         var state0 = {a: arg0, b: arg1};","         var cb0 = (arg0, arg1) => {"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/cli/tests/reference/async-import.wat","lines":["@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@","   (import \"./reference_test_bg.js\" \"__wbg_async_string_855e